{"text": "Cynthia Trinidad Sheahan Ed.S\nInterdisciplinary Bilingual Educator/Leader K-12\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\nDirector of Secondary Education and Educator Effectiveness\nOctober 2016- PRESENT\nAdams 14 School District\nSupervise, evaluate and coach secondary building principals\nCoach and advise building principals on writing, implementing and monitoring of\nUnified Improvement Plan\nFacilitate creation of high school course description and graduation requirements.\nMonitor budgets of all secondary schools.\nPartnered and collaborated with Chief Academic Officer on instructional\npractices and vertical articulation K-12\nDeveloping systems and structures for teacher/principal induction\nDeveloped and monitored district mentor/mentee program\nDeveloped professional development district wide that aligned with the District\nUnified Improvement Plan and Turnaround plan\nCreated and shepherd the implementation of district professional development\nprogramming K-12th grades\nTrained and monitored district on teacher/principal evaluation program\n\nDirector of Language Development\nJune 2014-October 2016\nBoulder Valley School District-Director of Language Development\n\nDevelop systems and structures district wide for ELL students and Bilingual\nprogramming\nObserved and evaluated building programs and district ELD program to comply with\n\nthe Office of Civil Right\nCreated and implemented protocol for identifying language learners who may also\nhave a learning disability to prevent over identification\nResearched and reviewed data of all ELL students K-12 grade in all 56 BVSD\nschools\nResearched and reviewed data to implement Cohort of buildings to participate in\ntraining by the Centered of Applied Linguistics (CAL)\nResearched and reviewed student count of ELL students to accurately report to\n\nColorado Department of Education\n\nSKILLS\n\nBilingual/Bilicultural Educator\nEquity Specialist\nLeadership development\nIntervention specialist\n\nParent and Community Engagement\nSpecialist\n\nAWARDS\nHispanic Advisory for embracing\ndiversity 2002-2003\nTeacher of the Month Brighton City of\ncommerce 2005\nRecognized by 9NEWS for Black\nHistory instruction 2005\nRecognized by Prairie View High School\nInaugural class for Most Influential\nteacher 2009\nKeynote Speaker CU-Bueno HEP GED\ngraduation 2011\nPresenter La Raza Youth Leadership\nConference 2012\nPresenter: CABE(Colorado Association\nof Bilingual Educators) Conference 2014\nCo-Chair of CO-ALAS (Colorado\nAdministrators and Superintendents of\nColorado) 2015-2016\n\nLANGUAGES\nEnglish/Spanish:Fluent in reading,\nwriting, speaking and listening",
